! The Session Contract ~ the record

The contract speaks at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract`>>; its dated rulings stand in that meme's <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/rulings`>>, and what the code holds stands in its <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/standing-and-owed`>>. This record keeps the owed debts and the history.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/owed`>>

!! Owed ~ for the kahu road

''OWED ~ eleven debts, each resting on the one before it.'' A builder closes each with its callers and its own proof, so the tree keeps a runnable contract at every step.

# ''Scoped document access.'' The session-scoped view over announcements, fetches, writes, catalog and content-addressed reads; no durable per-island store. The view, the pool's surface door and the island's half stand specified in code. The debt closes when every interactive surface mounts through that door, which waits on a verified face (debt two) and on callers that hold a session (debts four and six). Four hunks close with it: the share verdict's caller reads the pool's view for an island's peer, the leaf's relay adapter wears the one-way gate over its hearth's canon, the hearth wears that gate's twin toward its leaves, and a wiki island's verbs that read the catalog document move to the view's catalog ask.
# ''The face proof and its grants.'' Two faces on one vessel present different proof subjects, and a copied id or an own-hand claim gains no plane (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof`>>). The subjects, private authority, the session signer and the one face supplier stand specified in code. The debt closes when the node's session open on the local socket and the browser holder call the supplier and mint a signer at every open. Those callers wait on three things: the custody records for the face proof key and each vessel's face-scoped key, an admit that signs what it carries, and the ring's lookup by face subject (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/owed`>>). The supplier's face names one PersonaGroup at one Nexus, and a session binds that one (face, Nexus): a face that stands at a second Nexus opens a second session with its own proof and recipe, and no implicit multi-Nexus face session exists (a house ruling the operator MAY overturn).
# ''The recipe resolver and the pool's identity.'' The working-layer binding follows <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-working-layer`>>; two same-face sessions take two islands, a repeated exact mount opens one, and a recipe write reaches the next mount by sync without changing a live mount. The resolver and the whole-key pool stand specified in code, with one proof through the node vessel's own parts that a recipe naming an offering resolves. The working layer's address stands (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-working-layer`>>). The callers stay owed: the compose sites resolve the working kind through the slot-doc resolver's workbench port (the wiki's realm workbench); the compose sites resolve through the one function at surface mount, the browser's plugin selection folds into it, and the wiki door, its retained mount specs and the recipe watch retire with the last caller.
# ''Node callers move to sessions.'' The socket, its binding, the face-bound receipts and the local connector stand (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/standing-and-owed`>>). The node's production door answers `session:open` from the face supplier at either anchor, and every store-door verb and sealed act that acts as a face rides a session bound to that face (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands`>>); the debt closes once two CLI sessions wear different faces at once over one Repo, each judged by its own face's provider (the next lane), and a copied socket and a cross-face receipt read both refuse.
# ''The browser holder as owner.'' Two tabs show one backing Repo and one held lock; a failed daemon boot refuses both, releases the lock and permits a retry. The routing and the faceless envelope stand (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/standing-and-owed`>>). The browser holds one owner per store and each tab its own session through the vessel worker's port broker (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/browser-vessel-lift`>>). The face-bearing `session:open`, `session:call` and `session:switch` wait on the face supplier's browser caller, `W4` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-loops`>>), and the holder's custody fork waits on the operator.
# ''Browser surfaces.'' Two tabs mount one wiki under separate sessions; frames and control answers reach their source surface alone; no wiki engine runs on the page's main thread.
# ''The switch, and the selector retires.'' Switching one session leaves another live; an old generation's effect never paints the new face; no boot path reads a vessel-wide active face. The node's half stands (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands`>>); the browser's switch waits on `W4`.
# ''The disk as a surface.'' The watcher opens a session and leases each projected wiki; a disk edit returns under the leasing session's face; an edit from an earlier generation and a file changed under no lease both surface as drafts; a move between two faces' folders asks for a copy by name.
# ''The seat.'' An MCP connection opens a session under a standing grant, verified at each open and refused at the floor; its profile writes the working layer alone.
# ''The Mask as authorship.'' A record written into a shared realm carries its kind of hand, and a spirit's Mask, as a field no gate reads; a session cannot write another hand's mark.
# ''Door parity at the session.'' A CLI run and an MCP connection open the same session kinds and draw the same named refusals; a seat's refused verb names its profile; a seat drafts an authority act and cannot sign one; a sub-spirit's profile never exceeds its parent's.

* ''The profile-verb table'' (the hands room's profile lane): the node seat checks a session's face and anchor on `session:call` and `session:act`, never its profile, until the profile-verb table gates both.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/history`>>

!! History

* Before the daemon held one Keyhive provider per joined face, a daemon that booted one face's Keyhive provider judged a second face's session as the stranger its atom read as, until the next lane routed each session to its face's own provider.
* `persona wear` stood as a vessel-wide default-face verb before the one-shot CLI command named its face (operator ruling 2026-10-11).

<<~/ahu>>

